00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560


1
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,870
Today we'll derive the velocity vectors

2
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:09,870
for the motion of a particle in circular motion,

3
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:13,010
and we'll do so in polar coordinate system.

4
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:15,420
In polar coordinate system, the position vector

5
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:18,180
is this vector r, defined from the origin

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:23,710
of your coordinate system to the position of the particle.

7
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:27,630
The unit vector would be these r hat vector,

8
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:31,950
which is radially outward, and is theta hat vector, which

9
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:37,450
is tangential and perpendicular to the r hat direction.

10
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:40,900
We'll assume here that the motion of the particle

11
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,960
is confined to this circle of radius r.

12
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,830


13
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:52,110
The implication being that then this position vector

14
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:54,300
would have a constant magnitude, which

15
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,280
is the radius of this circle.

16
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,935
And we'll call this r without the vector notation.

17
00:00:58,935 --> 00:01:01,820


18
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,319
So in polar coordinate system, our position vector

19
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:09,070
can simply be written as this magnitude r in the r hat

20
00:01:09,070 --> 00:01:10,800
direction.

21
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,000
To get the velocity, then, we take the time derivative

22
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,200
of this position vector.

23
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,940


24
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:25,280
The magnitude r being a constant with time

25
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:28,010
will come out of the derivative, but we

26
00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:30,830
will take the time derivative then of this r hat vector.

27
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:34,050


28
00:01:34,050 --> 00:01:38,790
In polar coordinate system, this time derivative of r hat

29
00:01:38,790 --> 00:01:42,630
is not trivial because the direction of r hat changes

30
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:44,050
with time.

31
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:46,350
So at a later time, for instance,

32
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:51,420
when the particle is over here, the r hat direction

33
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,820
will be radially outward this way,

34
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,350
and the theta hat direction will be here.

35
00:01:56,350 --> 00:02:00,270
So both r hat and theta hat will constantly change direction

36
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:03,040
as a function of time.

37
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:08,160
So to calculate an expression for this dr hat dt,

38
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:10,380
we had previously derived a relationship

39
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:13,760
between the r hat and theta hat unit vectors,

40
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,650
with i hat and j hat, our unit vectors

41
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:20,850
in Cartesian coordinates system, which do not change with time.

42
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:27,210
We've established that r hat is a rotation from the i hat

43
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:31,850
direction, meaning that this r hat

44
00:02:31,850 --> 00:02:36,270
direction is a rotation of an angle theta from the x-axis.

45
00:02:36,270 --> 00:02:40,310
So similarly, then, the theta hat direction,

46
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:42,740
which is perpendicular to the r hat direction,

47
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:45,920
will be a rotation of an angle theta with respect

48
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:48,220
to the j hat direction.

49
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,860
We then derive that r hat is going

50
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:55,820
to have a component of cosine theta in the i hat

51
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:58,400
direction, that's this component, plus sine

52
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:03,740
of theta in the j hat direction, which is this component.

53
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:07,800
And theta hat is going to have a component in the minus i hat

54
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:12,770
direction, which is in minus sine of theta,

55
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:17,660
plus a component in the j hat direction, which

56
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:22,850
is this adjacent, which is cosine theta in the j hat

57
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:25,280
direction.

58
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:28,530
So from this expression, we can take the time derivative,

59
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:33,600
dr hat dt, the derivative of cosine

60
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:36,570
giving us minus sine of theta, and because theta

61
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:40,240
can change as a function of time,

62
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:43,630
then we have to do a chain rule to get d theta dt,

63
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:46,320
that is, this, the derivative of this expression,

64
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:48,570
in the i hat direction.

65
00:03:48,570 --> 00:03:51,870
And the derivative of sine theta is

66
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:56,860
going to be cosine of theta, and by the chain rule, d theta dt,

67
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:00,010
in the j hat direction.

68
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:04,110
So by taking the time derivative of this r hat vector, in fact,

69
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:09,340
we pick up a d theta dt, and the remaining expression,

70
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:12,660
minus sine of theta in the i hat direction, plus cosine

71
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:17,800
of theta in the j hat direction, is exactly what theta hat is.

72
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:22,570


73
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:27,650
This expression, in parentheses, is exactly what theta hat is.

74
00:04:27,650 --> 00:04:31,840
So the time derivative of the r hat dt

75
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:35,668
gives us d theta dt in the theta hat direction.

76
00:04:35,668 --> 00:04:38,300


77
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:40,910
Now that we've derived an expression for the time

78
00:04:40,910 --> 00:04:45,140
derivative of dr hat dt, we are ready to continue

79
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:47,300
our derivation for the velocity.

80
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:51,190


81
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:54,270
Then the time derivative of the position vector,

82
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:56,610
which gives us the velocity, is r,

83
00:04:56,610 --> 00:05:00,810
which is a constant, times the time derivative of r hat,

84
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:04,090
and the time derivative of r hat gives us a d theta

85
00:05:04,090 --> 00:05:08,960
dt, in the theta hat direction.

86
